Appended by a dafoam `lab-lane` on the dafoam-supervisor's brief, under Sanaa's
`docs/SANAA_DIRECTIVE_2026-09-12_RUN_INSTRUCTIONS.md`. **Nothing above is rewritten; §0–§8 stand
verbatim.** This revision (a) closes one of §8's three open questions with arithmetic, (b) adds one
**mandatory** carry-forward the supervisor's brief directs, (c) records Sanaa's launch preconditions
per level, and (d) reports a measured mesh inventory that changes what R2 costs. **It sets no gate,
moves no threshold and grades nothing. No R2 compute has run.**

## 9. §8 QUESTION 2 CLOSED — THE §5 MEMORY GUARD FOR `R2-L1`

§5 registered the guard as owed and named it "the real risk at 6.39M cells is memory, not cost".
The box has since changed under it.

| | old box (when §5 was drafted) | now |
|---|---|---|
| instance | 30 GiB total | **r7a.4xlarge, 16 cores, 123 GiB** |
| MemAvailable | `available=0 GiB` repeatedly 13:41–17:25 (`SOLVE_L2.gatedlaunch.log`); 1.42 GiB at 10:11 | **120 GiB**, swap 15 GiB **0 used** |

**Registered guard for `R2-L1`, and it is a refusal to START, never a cap:**

| | value |
|---|---|
| container ceiling | **`--memory 40g --memory-swap 40g`** — swap DISABLED (Sanaa item 18) |
| `MemAvailable` required to start | **48 GiB** (ceiling + 8 GiB host headroom) |
| below it | the level does **not start**; it is `BLOCKED`, not squeezed — **§5's own word, unchanged** |

**Basis, and its confidence stated honestly.** The primal at 6,389,760 cells is `DARhoSimpleCFoam`
at np = 8, decomposed, so per-rank footprint is ~1/8 of the whole. The measured sibling is A3GC-L2 at
798,720 cells on the same solver, and the lab holds no RSS reading for it. **40 GiB is therefore a
bound, not a measurement, and is labelled so.** It is ~8× the total this family's 1.6M-cell level
could plausibly need, on a box with 120 GiB free, which makes generosity free. **The first R2 level
to run measures the real figure and the calibration row carries it.**

**Why this is not a cap.** It never signals, throttles or shortens a running solver. It refuses to
start when starting would take memory a live sibling relies on — the identical structure as
`MP_A5R` ADDENDUM 1 §A1.5, and it is compatible with Sanaa's directive #17 for the same reason.

> §8's other two questions are **NOT** closed here and are not a lane's to close: whether the §6.1
> `a3gc_grade_R2_GFIELD.diff` is applied (the supervisor's personal diff read,
> `SUPERVISION_CHARTER.md` §3 check 1, not delegable), and whether R2 supersedes A3GC.

## 10. §4.7 — `G-RESREAD`: **THE RESIDUAL READER IS MANDATED, NOT LEFT TO THE GRADER**

**Binding on every R2 arm, and on any A3GC arm that runs with non-orthogonal correctors on.**

`a3gc_grade.py:700-701` assigns per-equation initial residuals **in a loop that overwrites**, so it
returns the **LAST** match in the last `Time =` block. `DAUtility::primalResidualControl` is called
**inside** `while (simple.correctNonOrthogonal())` (`pEqnSimple.H:41,52`) and prints one
`<eq> initRes:` line **per corrector**. With correctors on, the last line is the final corrector's
initial residual — measured off an almost-solved field — which says nothing about whether the
**outer** iteration converged. **Demonstrated 2026-09-12: that reader read back a planted
`1.234e-09` as though it had passed.**

**The required reader is FIRST MATCH PER EQUATION PER BLOCK**, and it already exists, already frozen,
already controlled:

| | |
|---|---|
| file | `cases/dafoam/ladder-a/A3/curriculum_A3GC/a3gc_grade_l2r.py` |
| md5 | **`b188e7e1b0034a53267dc9b818138b8c`** |
| freeze | **`5eaa652fa`** |
| the clause | `:699-729`, `for eq, val in _INITRES_RE.findall(tail): if eq not in last: last[eq] = float(val)` |
| its control | three-direction, on L2's **own** artifacts, with the two fixtures `A3GC_L2R_FIXTURE_{single,multi}corrector.log` beside it |

**REUSE IT. DO NOT REWRITE IT.** A second implementation of a clause this specific is a second thing
to get wrong, and the existing one carries a control a rewrite would have to re-earn.

**Why FIRST is right by construction and not by luck** (the reader's own reasoning, carried here so
the registration states it rather than pointing at it): FIRST is the outer iteration's initial
residual **before any corrector has acted**, which is exactly what "has this outer iteration
converged" means. The maximum would *usually* coincide, because the first corrector normally carries
the largest residual — but "usually" is a property of the arithmetic on a given day, not of the
definition. **And the direction is one-way: this reader returns the residual before the correctors
reduced it, so it reads the HARDER number. THIS CLAUSE CAN ONLY LOWER A VERDICT, NEVER RAISE ONE.**

**It binds R2 even though R2 registers `nNonOrthogonalCorrectors 0`** (§7: settings held
byte-identical to the validated tutorial). With zero correctors each equation prints once per block
and FIRST ≡ LAST, so the clause costs nothing and changes no number **today**. It is registered
anyway, because §7 registers `nNonOrthogonalCorrectors` as an explicit **lever** that any level
failing §4.4 may pull — and the moment that lever is pulled, the `LAST` reader silently starts
returning a number that cannot fail. **A guard installed after the lever is pulled is a guard
installed after the accident.**

## 11. SANAA'S LAUNCH PRECONDITIONS FOR R2

| item | state |
|---|---|
| **6 — ubuntu, never root** | **SATISFIED BY A MEASURED SPELLING: `-u 1000:1000 --group-add 1002 -e MPLCONFIGDIR=/tmp`.** **uid 1000 and gid 1000 are both `ubuntu`**, so every artifact lands `ubuntu:ubuntu`; 1002 is the *image's* `dafoamuser` group carried as a **supplementary** group for one purpose only — traversing the 0750 `/home/dafoamuser`. Measured on this box 2026-09-12: `-u 1000:1000` **alone** dies `Permission denied` sourcing `loadDAFoam.sh`; with `--group-add 1002` it reaches `LOADED_OK` and `id` reads `uid=1000(ubuntu) gid=1000(ubuntu) groups=1000(ubuntu),1002(dafoamuser)`. **Corroborated by a live peer run on the same image** — container `d6r2c_KR_REF_20260912T184838Z_79250`, `User=1000:1000`, `GroupAdd=["1002"]`, solving. **This supersedes `a3gc_genmesh.sh:66-67`'s `-u 1002:1000` for every R2 instrument**, because 1002 is a uid that does not exist on the host and leaves artifacts owned by a numeric stranger. *(Correction recorded: this lane first proposed `-u 1000:1002`; it works, but moves the primary group to a gid with no host user. The better spelling is the peer lane's.)* |
| **7 — memory declared** | Per level: R2-L3 **8 GiB**, R2-L2 **16 GiB**, R2-L1 **40 GiB** ceilings, floors +8 GiB. R2-L3's is bounded by the anchor, which ran at 399,360 cells np=4 on a 30 GiB box beside other work. **Bounds, not measurements**, labelled so; the first level to run replaces them. |
| **8 — core guard** | np = **8** per level (the rate table's basis). 8 solver ranks + fleet ≤ 16. **The three levels are a WAVE, not three concurrent runs** — §6.3 already orders them L3 → L2 → L1, and the runner launches at most one entry per tick. |
| **1–3 — checkpoints** | **REGISTERED, AND IT IS A CHANGE THE FAMILY NEEDS.** `endTime 6000` at the anchor's measured rate is 81.4 core-min at np=4 ≈ 20 min wall at np=8 for L3, but ≈ **2.7 h for L1** (§5). L1 therefore **must** checkpoint: `writeInterval` **500** iterations, which at the §5 rate is ≈ 13 min of wall at L1 and never exceeds Sanaa's 30 minutes; `purgeWrite 2`, keeping the last two and purging older, exactly as her item 1 requires. **L3 and L2 carry the same 500 for family identity** — a family whose levels differ in `controlDict` is one more uncontrolled variable, which is the entire defect R2 exists to repair. **This is a departure from the anchor's `writeInterval`, is registered here BEFORE any R2 compute, and must be read back off each level's `controlDict` at launch, not assumed.** |
| **5 — kill-and-resume proof** | **OWED AND NOT RUN.** R2's class is steady OpenFOAM (`DARhoSimpleCFoam` in a container). R2-L3 at ≈ 81 core-min is the cheapest place to run it. Not claimed, not assumed. |
| **9 — detached** | The runner's `setsid nohup` wrapper with rc captured inside it. |
| **10 — frozen before launch** | **NOT YET. THIS FILE IS A DRAFT.** §4.5's bands and §5's costs are drafted; §8 questions 1 and 3 are open; the freeze is the supervisor's act. |
| **17/18 — box hygiene** | Read at drafting: load far under 16 after the 17:36Z reboot; MemAvailable 120 GiB; swap 0 used. Not a substitute for the runner's reading at launch. |

