Probed read-only with `a3gc_grade.py probe` on 2026-09-12, against trees this lane did not produce:

| R2 level | registered cells / wing faces | already on disk? | where |
|---|---|---|---|
| **R2-L3** (c2 × 64) | 399,360 / 6,240 | **YES — in three places, all probing EXACTLY 399360 / 6240** | `A3GC-AR1`, `A3GC-AR1C`, `A3-onera-m6-transonic` |
| **R2-L2** (c1 × 64) | 1,597,440 / 24,960 | **NO — nowhere on the box** | (A3GC-L2 is c1 × **32** = 798,720 / 24,960 — same surface, half the layers) |
| **R2-L1** (c0 × 64) | 6,389,760 / 99,840 | **ONE STEP AWAY** | `A3GC-L1`: pyHyp output preserved (437,206,919 B); only `plot3dToFoam` onward is owed |

**R2-L1 and A3GC-L1 are the SAME MESH.** A3GC's `L1` is `COARSEN_PASSES 0`, `N_LAYERS 65` →
6,389,760 cells (`a3gc_genmesh.sh:79-81`), and R2-L1 is c0 × 64 wall-normal cells → 6,389,760. The
parameters are identical, so the mesh is. **The interrupted conversion in
`A3GC_L1_REENTRY_PREREGISTRATION.md.DRAFT`, once finished, delivers R2's fine level and the ~896
core-min of pyHyp already spent on it is not repaid.**

> **A REGISTRATION QUESTION THIS LANE DOES NOT DECIDE, AND FLAGS RATHER THAN ASSUMES.** §6.2 rules
> that no pre-existing *level* is adopted into R2. A **mesh** is an input generated in stage 1, not a
> graded run, and the three probes above are coordinate-level counts rather than provenance — but
> §6.2's reasoning ("adopting a completed level into a family frozen afterwards is precisely what
> rule 2 exists to prevent") is close enough that **the supervisor must rule explicitly on whether
> R2 may consume pre-freeze meshes**, per level. If the ruling is no, R2-L3 and R2-L1 regenerate from
> the family script and §5's cost table gains stage-1 time it does not currently carry. **Reading
> §6.2 either way without saying so would be the lane deciding a registration question.**

**Consequence for the queue, either way: only `R2-L2` needs a mesh that exists nowhere**, and no
generator table entry for `c1 × 64 layers` exists — `a3gc_genmesh.sh`'s tables carry L3/L2/L1/AR1 and
none of them is it. **That instrument change is the supervisor's**, and it lands on a file whose
AMENDMENT 5 md5 pin is *already* stale (pin `9fa240d9…`, disk and HEAD `2a1f45c0…` since commit
`8b16844fa`), which must be repaired in the same act or `a3gc_L1_wrapper.sh` keeps refusing at
`exit 90`.

